---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Free Markdown Tools - Online Editor, Converter, Cheat Sheet & More | MarkdownMaster"
  description="Free online Markdown tools: real-time editor, Markdown to HTML converter, syntax reference, cheat sheet, and documentation. No sign-up required."
  canonical="https://markdownmaster.site/tools/"
>
  <style>
    .tools-hero {
      text-align:center; padding:4rem 1.5rem 2rem;
      background: linear-gradient(180deg, #0f172a 0%, #1e293b 50%, #0f172a 100%);
      position:relative; overflow:hidden;
    }
    .tools-hero h1 { font-size:clamp(1.75rem,4vw,2.75rem); font-weight:800; letter-spacing:-0.03em; }
    .tools-hero p { color:var(--text-dim); max-width:600px; margin:0.75rem auto 0; line-height:1.7; }

    .tools-grid { max-width:1100px; margin:0 auto; padding:2.5rem 1.5rem 4rem; }
    .tools-subtitle { text-align:center; color:var(--text-muted); margin-bottom:2rem; font-size:0.9rem; }
    .tgrid { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(300px,1fr)); gap:1rem; }
    .tcard {
      display:flex; flex-direction:column; background:var(--bg-card); border:1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius:12px; padding:1.75rem; text-decoration:none; color:var(--text);
      transition:all 0.15s;
    }
    .tcard:hover { border-color:var(--accent); transform:translateY(-2px); }
    .tcard-icon { width:44px; height:44px; background:rgba(14,165,233,0.12); border-radius:10px; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; font-size:1.4rem; margin-bottom:1rem; }
    .tcard h3 { font-size:1rem; font-weight:600; margin-bottom:0.4rem; }
    .tcard p { font-size:0.85rem; color:var(--text-dim); line-height:1.7; flex:1; }
    .tcard-cta { margin-top:0.75rem; font-weight:600; color:var(--accent); font-size:0.85rem; }

    .tsection { max-width:800px; margin:0 auto; padding:0 1.5rem 3rem; }
    .tsection h2 { font-size:1.5rem; font-weight:700; margin-bottom:1rem; text-align:center; }
    .tsection p { color:var(--text-dim); line-height:1.8; margin-bottom:1rem; font-size:0.95rem; }

    @media (max-width: 640px) { .tgrid { grid-template-columns:1fr; } }
  </style>

  <section class="tools-hero">
    <h1>Free Markdown Tools</h1>
    <p>Everything you need to write, preview, convert, and master Markdown — all free, no sign-up required.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="tools-grid">
    <p class="tools-subtitle">Choose a tool to get started instantly.</p>
    <div class="tgrid">
      <a href="/templates/" class="tcard">
        <div class="tcard-icon">&#x1F9E9;</div>
        <h3>Markdown Templates</h3>
        <p>Start a GitHub README, API reference, command guide, release note, technical brief, or comparison table with a practical Markdown structure.</p>
        <span class="tcard-cta">Browse free templates &rarr;</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/tools/markdown-to-html/" class="tcard">
        <div class="tcard-icon">&#x21C4;</div>
        <h3>Markdown to HTML Converter</h3>
        <p>Convert Markdown to clean HTML instantly, then copy the output. Runs privately in your browser.</p>
        <span class="tcard-cta">Convert Markdown to HTML &rarr;</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/tools/markdown-table-generator/" class="tcard">
        <div class="tcard-icon">&#x25A6;</div>
        <h3>Markdown Table Generator</h3>
        <p>Build GitHub Flavored Markdown tables with editable cells, then copy the exact syntax you need.</p>
        <span class="tcard-cta">Create a Markdown table &rarr;</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/tools/readme-generator/" class="tcard">
        <div class="tcard-icon">&#x1F4C3;</div>
        <h3>GitHub README Generator</h3>
        <p>Turn your project details into a clear, structured README template ready to copy into a repository.</p>
        <span class="tcard-cta">Generate a README &rarr;</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/editor/" class="tcard">
        <div class="tcard-icon">&#x270F;&#xFE0F;</div>
        <h3>Markdown Editor</h3>
        <p>Real-time Markdown editor with live preview, syntax highlighting, GFM support, and HTML export. Write and preview instantly.</p>
        <span class="tcard-cta">Open Editor &rarr;</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/docs/" class="tcard">
        <div class="tcard-icon">&#x1F4D6;</div>
        <h3>Markdown Syntax Reference</h3>
        <p>Complete Markdown syntax guide covering headings, bold, italic, links, images, tables, code blocks, lists, and all GFM extensions.</p>
        <span class="tcard-cta">View Docs &rarr;</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/blog/markdown-cheat-sheet-complete-guide/" class="tcard">
        <div class="tcard-icon">&#x1F4DD;</div>
        <h3>Markdown Cheat Sheet</h3>
        <p>Quick-reference cheat sheet covering every Markdown syntax element with examples. Perfect for beginners and experienced users alike.</p>
        <span class="tcard-cta">View Cheat Sheet &rarr;</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/blog/what-is-markdown-complete-beginners-guide/" class="tcard">
        <div class="tcard-icon">&#x1F393;</div>
        <h3>What Is Markdown? Beginner's Guide</h3>
        <p>New to Markdown? Start here. Learn what Markdown is, why it is used by millions, and how to write your first Markdown document.</p>
        <span class="tcard-cta">Learn Markdown &rarr;</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/blog/markdown-syntax-complete-guide/" class="tcard">
        <div class="tcard-icon">&#x1F4C4;</div>
        <h3>Complete Markdown Syntax Guide</h3>
        <p>Every Markdown rule, extension, and feature explained with examples — from basic formatting to advanced features like footnotes, Mermaid diagrams, and math formulas.</p>
        <span class="tcard-cta">Read Guide &rarr;</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/blog/markdown-tables-how-to-create-format-align/" class="tcard">
        <div class="tcard-icon">&#x1F4CA;</div>
        <h3>Markdown Tables Guide</h3>
        <p>How to create, format, and align tables in Markdown. Full syntax reference with alignment options, advanced formatting, and common pitfalls.</p>
        <span class="tcard-cta">Master Tables &rarr;</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/blog/markdown-links-images-complete-guide/" class="tcard">
        <div class="tcard-icon">&#x1F517;</div>
        <h3>Markdown Links &amp; Images Guide</h3>
        <p>Complete guide to adding links, images, and reference-style links in Markdown. Covers inline links, auto-links, clickable images, and footnotes.</p>
        <span class="tcard-cta">Read Guide &rarr;</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/blog/markdown-for-developers-readme-docs-wikis/" class="tcard">
        <div class="tcard-icon">&#x1F4BB;</div>
        <h3>Markdown for Developers</h3>
        <p>How to use Markdown for GitHub READMEs, API documentation, project wikis, and technical writing. Practical developer-focused guide.</p>
        <span class="tcard-cta">Read for Devs &rarr;</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/blog/how-to-convert-markdown-to-html/" class="tcard">
        <div class="tcard-icon">&#x1F504;</div>
        <h3>Markdown to HTML Converter Guide</h3>
        <p>Learn how to convert Markdown to HTML using online tools and libraries. Includes step-by-step examples and a free online converter.</p>
        <span class="tcard-cta">Convert Now &rarr;</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/blog/how-to-use-ai-to-write-markdown/" class="tcard">
        <div class="tcard-icon">&#x1F916;</div>
        <h3>AI + Markdown Guide</h3>
        <p>Use ChatGPT, Claude, and Gemini to write Markdown faster. Practical prompts for docs, meeting notes, tables, and code blocks.</p>
        <span class="tcard-cta">Explore &rarr;</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/blog/markdown-vs-rich-text-editors-compared/" class="tcard">
        <div class="tcard-icon">&#x2696;&#xFE0F;</div>
        <h3>Markdown vs Rich Text Comparison</h3>
        <p>Markdown or WYSIWYG? Compare both formats across 8 key criteria and find out which one works best for your workflow.</p>
        <span class="tcard-cta">Compare &rarr;</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/blog/markdown-vs-html-when-to-use-which/" class="tcard">
        <div class="tcard-icon">&#x1F4AC;</div>
        <h3>Markdown vs HTML Guide</h3>
        <p>When to use Markdown vs HTML for writing content, documentation, and web pages. Real examples showing why Markdown wins for content creation.</p>
        <span class="tcard-cta">Read More &rarr;</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="tsection">
    <h2>More Markdown Resources</h2>
    <p>Browse our full collection of <a href="/blog/">Markdown tutorials, guides, and comparisons</a>. Whether you are just getting started or looking to master advanced features like footnotes, Mermaid diagrams, and math formulas, we have a guide for you.</p>
    <p>All tools are <strong>100% free</strong>, run entirely in your browser, and require no account or sign-up. Your content stays private and never leaves your device.</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
